        <description><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;">​A <strong>Workplace Harassment and Violence Risk Assessment</strong> is a structured process used to identify, assess, and mitigate risks related to harassment and violence in the workplace. It’s designed to ensure a safe and respectful working environment for all employees. This assessment is a legal requirement and should be done every tree years, following a Notice of Occurrence with a third party or whenever significant changes occur in the workplace. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;">The designated employer representative must complete this assessment, in collaboration with the Workplace Health and Safety Committee.</span></p>
<p><strong><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;">Please complete the template below and attach it to the mandatory attachment clip at the end of this form.</span></strong></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #3598db;"><a style="color: #3598db;" href="/sys_attachment.do?sys_id&#61;a2f78ac63b719290aeb1ebc964e45a12" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Workplace Harassment and Violence Risk Assessment</a> </span></p>]]></description>
